course: dictionary
lesson: 9591
title: Strengthen: making things stronger
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To strengthen something is to make it stronger. When you meet this word, look at the words around it for clues. «Exercises that strengthen your legs» tells you that the exercises make your legs stronger.
explain: Strengthen can also be used for feelings, ideas and friendships. «Arguing with respect can keep and even strengthen friendships.» Friendships are not made of metal, so strengthen here means making them firmer and more certain.
explain: Try the swap. Put "make stronger" in place of strengthen and check that the sentence still makes sense. In «A scout ant leaves a smell trail from food to the nest; others follow and strengthen it», the ants make the trail stronger, so other ants can follow it while the food lasts.
fact: Strengthen is a verb: strengthen, strengthens, strengthened, strengthening.
fact: «Strengthen» means to make something stronger, or to become stronger.
fact: «Strengthen» can also mean to make a feeling, idea or friendship firmer or more certain.
fact: Strength is the noun, and strong is the adjective it comes from.
fact: Bridges and frames are often strengthened with extra supports, such as triangles.
exercise: «Sport strengthens the tummy and back muscles that hold you up.» What does strengthens mean here? | Puts away | Makes softer | *Makes stronger | Makes it hurt more
exercise: What does strengthen mean in «Arguing with respect can keep and even strengthen friendships»? | Makes friendships quieter | Ends friendships | Counts how many friendships there are | *Makes friendships firmer and more certain
exercise: Which word is the -ing form of strengthen? | strong | strengthened | *strengthening | strengths
test: «A physiotherapist gives exercises to bend and strengthen the arm a bit more each week.» Strengthen here means? | To paint the arm | To rest the arm completely | *To make the arm stronger | To break the arm
test: Which word is the past tense of strengthen? | strengthening | strengthens | strengthen | *strengthened
exam: Which use of strengthen is about a friendship? | Sport strengthens the tummy muscles | A physiotherapist gives exercises | *Arguing with respect can keep and even strengthen friendships | A scout ant leaves a smell trail
